        <p>A contractor site earns trust differently from a retail site. The signals that matter most are: real project photos rather than stock images, a service area so prospects know whether you cover their location, contact details on every page, and testimonials from clients who name the type of work. Licensing or insurance details, if you choose to include them, signal that you operate in a regulated industry and take compliance seriously.</p>
        <p>A photo of your crew on a real job does more for credibility than any stock image of a hard hat. Buyers in the trades are experienced — they recognize a generic template the moment they land on it.</p>
